lines = {
"attor_1": {
"text": "Your continued behavior is garnering a lot of interest at court.",
"who": "A voice"
},
"attor_2": {
"text": "She has begun wondering—wondering why you haven't given up yet. And why four naga wound up dead not too long ago.",
"who": "A voice"
},
"attor_3": {
"text": "Though you have a heart of stone, Tamlin, you certainly keep a host of fear inside it.",
"who": "A voice"
},
"attor_4": {
"text": "All will be right as rain soon enough.",
"who": "A voice"
},
"lucien_burn": {
"text": "Burn in Hell.",
"who": "Lucien"
},
"tamlin_gone": {
"text": "It's gone.",
"who": "Tamlin"
},
"tamlin_reply": {
"text": "Tell her I'm getting sick of cleaning up the trash she dumps on my borders.",
"who": "Tamlin"
},
"tamlin_stay": {
"text": "Stay hidden, and no matter what you overhear, don't come out.",
"who": "Tamlin"
}
}
extra_require = PackedStringArray()
invented = PackedStringArray()
canon = "Ch19 (Keeper, 2026-11-02, book-checked). DAYTIME ('despite the warmth of the day'). Walking back into the gardens on a gravel path, the garden goes horribly still. Tamlin snarls 'Stay hidden, and no matter what you overhear, don't come out' and is gone; there is NO push: she ducks behind a hedge herself and nearly bolts for the stables but freezes. Through dense leaves she watches Tamlin and Lucien face someone invisible: a low, disembodied, deep and sibilant voice, a hiss, a chuckle like sand shifting; at the end a flap of leathery wings, a foul wind, silence; then Tamlin: 'It's gone.' Every line here is [V] (Keeper-confirmed wording). Tamlin's glamour hid her from it (ch24). X: the yew pocket on the lawn west of the arbor (open to the east, toward Tamlin; clear of the house's walled walk, which runs x -42..-38 from the terrace), the rustle/detection mechanic and its permanent fact, the gravel pressed by unseen feet. Marks are in the attor_hiding_spot anchor's frame (-40, -105.5, under the arbor near the house; -Z faces the rose garden)."
